course: dictionary
lesson: 7315
title: Placement: finding the right place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Placement comes from place. It means putting something in a certain spot, or finding the right spot for someone. Context tells you which meaning you need, so read the words around it. «The placement of the furniture» is about where things are put in a room.
explain: For people, placement means finding a place for them, such as a school, a job or a home. «Not every placement works.» The clue is that a place was chosen for someone and it did not suit them. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "Not every place chosen for someone works" make sense? Yes, so you have it.
explain: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a work placement is a short time in a workplace to gain experience. Notice that placement can mean a place, a position, or a period of training. Context is what decides which one you are reading.
fact: Placement is a noun, and its plural is placements.
fact: «Placement» means putting something in a certain place or position.
fact: A «placement test» decides the right class or level for a pupil.
fact: A «work placement» is a short job or training time in a workplace, used to gain experience (UK, Ireland, Australia).
fact: «Product placement» means a brand shown in a film, often because the company paid for it to be there.
exercise: «Not every placement works.» What does placement mean in this sentence? | A kind of sports game | A paint colour | * A place or arrangement chosen for someone | A tiny coin
exercise: A «work placement» is best described as: | * A short time in a workplace to gain experience | A race around the park | A holiday in a foreign country | A type of jumper
exercise: Why does the placement of commas matter in a sentence? | Commas make sentences longer | Commas are only used in poems | * Where they go can change the meaning | Commas are always the same, so placement does not matter
test: «A placement test» helps decide which class or level is right for a pupil. What does it decide? | How long lunch will be | * The right class or level | The colour of the classroom walls
test: A brand of soda in a film is often «product placement». What does this mean? | The film was shot in a shop | * The company paid for its drink to be shown there | A new kind of soda was invented that day | The actors chose the drink for themselves
exam: In «if a placement isn't safe, tell a social worker or teacher», placement most likely means: | A small coin | * An arrangement where a child lives or learns | A type of paint | A sports game played outside
